{# The docked rails an editor opens on the right of what is being written: one for the
   component the cursor is in, one for the link, one for the files. Only ever one of them
   is open -- they share the slot -- and all three are declared here so that no template
   rendering an editor can ship some of them and not the others.

   Every template that renders an {{aceditor}} includes THIS, and nothing else: the
   editor's JavaScript builds all three rails on startup, so a page that shipped two of
   them used to break on the third. See javascripts/editor-rails.js.

   They belong OUTSIDE the edited form -- each carries inputs of its own, which configure
   what is being written rather than being fields of the page -- and, where there is one,
   inside .yw-designer as a sibling of the canvas. #}
